        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "ef5d49f761609c4b28ba4327c2a7342cba47a474",
            "parents": [
                "adfc21cc2d8acfe106b3b49f56dcb5fb38407a95"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/17/88817/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Tan Siewert",
                "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                "username": "sinuscosinustan"
            },
            "createdOn": 1774967299,
            "author": {
                "name": "Tan Siewert",
                "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                "username": "sinuscosinustan"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "```suggestion\n\nDecorator objects (with `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.Asset` interface) may be provided by devicetree-vpd-parser (via\nMachineContext) and used as probe, but then also get populated to the\n```\n\nassuming that's the interface you were talking about"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, done. Also clarified it a bit more because I seem to have mixed up some words in the D-Bus context."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "So your issue is that you need `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.Asset` interface on the actual inventory item (held by EM) instead of the object that the vpd parser produces.\n\nDoes your probe statement look like this by any chance?\n\n```\n    \"Name\": \"chassis\",\n    \"Probe\": \"xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.Asset({'Model': 'HPE ProLiant DL365 Gen11'})\",\n    \"Type\": \"Chassis\",\n    \"xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.Asset\": {\n        \"Manufacturer\": \"$Manufacturer\",\n        \"Model\": \"$Model\",\n        \"PartNumber\": \"$PartNumber\",\n        \"SerialNumber\": \"$SerialNumber\"\n    },\n```\n\nTo solve the immediate issue, is it possible to slightly change the property value of what you are probing on vs. what you expose?\n\n\ne.g.\n\n`    \"Probe\": \n\"xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.Asset(\n{'Model': 'HPE ProLiant DL365 Gen11-probe'})\",`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "?  The bug is in the above config.  You shouldn't be probing on Decorator.Asset interfaces.  I'm not against this change, but ultimately the bad config is the problem.  You should be probing on the specific API, not an asset API."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "@alexander.hansen@9elements.com Exactly. Changing the probe was an idea that I had too, but haven't looked too much into. will check it.\n\n\n@ed@tanous.net `devicetree-vpd-parser` exports the values on the `Decorator.Asset` interface [1], which is also defined in the design doc [2]. Another way to solve the issue would be either:\n- allowing to filter by D-Bus names in the Probe, or\n\n- move the properties from `devicetree-vpd-parser` into another interface, which in the end would require a change in the design.\n\n[1] https://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/d40558216ad85e99f3c37614fc96e088241a4f72/src/devicetree_vpd_parser/machine_context.hpp#L10-L16\n[2] https://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/49beca34959cb2922a0dede07da9ec52dc4f4be5/designs/entity-manager-hw-id-vpd-discover-via-device-tree.md?plain=1#L315-L325"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> exports the values on the Decorator.Asset interface\n\nOk, then it's the problem.  The intent of probed interfaces is that you're not probing on inventory, you're probing to CREATE the inventory.  This is also why the probable interfaces weren't added to PDI (wide debate if that was right)  If you can create the inventory directly, just do that and don't put the asset interface in EM at all."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "Sorry for the delay in response.\n\n\nWhile I agree with you that if `devicetree-vpd-parser` can create the inventory interface, we shouldn't create them in EM again. But: Even without this reasoning / my misuse here, it shouldn't be possible to do this on purpose as @spinler@us.ibm.com has already pointed out."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I assume this discussion is resolved since the config in question is no longer part of this patch as of the current patchset.\n\nCurrently it looks like a reasonable fix for EM."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "How did you confirm this behavior change will not cause problems for existing upstream configs?\n\nAre there upstream configs which probe on interfaces also exposed by EM, that would be impacted by this change?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not aware of any that work that way, and by design they shouldn't be."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "There are multiple upstream configurations which are probing on interfaces which (could be) exposed by EM.\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/d40558216ad85e99f3c37614fc96e088241a4f72/configurations/meta/bletchley/bletchley_frontpanel.json#L90\n\nis probing on `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.Asset`\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/d40558216ad85e99f3c37614fc96e088241a4f72/configurations/ibm/sbp1_rssd.json#L381\n\nis probing on `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item`\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/d40558216ad85e99f3c37614fc96e088241a4f72/configurations/ibm/tacoma_rack_controller.json#L20\n\nis probing on `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.Asset`\n\nAs a consequence, someone wanting to stop EM from probing it's own interfaces must check that in those instances the interface is not coming from EM. Otherwise risk of breaking stuff."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "There's only one config that I am unaware where it's coming from, and that is the Tacoma Rack controller. For all other configs I was able to figure out where it was coming from:\n\nBletchley: https://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/blob/991de8113f8deea0ffb2aade388aa19a36e0959d/meta-facebook/meta-bletchley/recipes-phosphor/settings/phosphor-settings-defaults-native/bletchley-frontpanel.yaml\n\nSBP1: https://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/blob/991de8113f8deea0ffb2aade388aa19a36e0959d/meta-ibm/meta-genesis3/recipes-phosphor/inventory/static-inventory/static-inventory.yaml#L1142\n\nTacoma Rack Controller: No idea."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Tacoma Rack Controller: No idea.\n\n@spinler@us.ibm.com can you confirm in this case where it is coming from.."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "It comes from xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Manager."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Well i guess that means my original concern has been resolved \ud83d\ude0a"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "This is not an upstream config, only DL360G12 is upstream, right?\n\n```\nls configurations/hpe/\ndl360g12_baseboard.json\n```\n\nso no one can really tell which problem you actually ran into, and if it is a real issue or just an instance of misconfiguration.\n\nPlease provide some permalink or concrete example.\n\nIs it \nhttps://github.com/canopybmc/canopybmc/blob/469720b37c74783f52806ef01dac67d880bf6e69/meta-canopy/meta-hpe/meta-common/recipes-phosphor/configuration/entity-manager/dl365g11_baseboard.json\n\nby any chance?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "Right... I forgot to add the reference here (yours is correct). Sorry about that! Fixed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 71,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Seems unrelated to this change."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 71,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "Mentioned in the commit description, since I use the D-Bus name of EM in a condition now it'd make sense to move it to a constant and also use it on the iface registration. If you don't agree with the change, then I'll drop it again."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 100,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
